{
  "_KIT_CLASS": "KIT — the opt-in unattended launch profile, as a shape. JSON has no comment syntax, so its classification marker is this KEY, the same carve-out settings.json.example states — process/EXTRACTION.md § The one file classification convention.",
  "_README": "Kit template — an ADDITIONAL settings file for a session nobody is watching (an overnight run, a scheduled one), passed at launch rather than copied to .claude/settings.json. It does not replace settings.json.example: the two are launched TOGETHER (the harness reads every settings source given to it). Naming which profile a launch uses is the adapter's job — process/templates/AGENTS-adapter.template.md § What is ON and what is OFF here.",

  "_WHAT_THIS_FILE_MAY_CONTAIN": "ONLY SETTINGS KEYS WHOSE EFFECT THE KIT CAN DEMONSTRATE — the same rule settings.json.example states. This file exists because TWO things clear that bar for an unattended launch: denying the harness's own interactive-question tool, verified to be enforced (not merely a hint) even under a permissive mode, by removing the tool from the model's context before any permission check runs; and a Stop hook that catches a turn ending on an unaddressed question.",

  "_WHY_A_SEPARATE_FILE_AND_NOT_A_KEY_IN_THE_BASE_ONE": "Denying the interactive-question tool, and blocking a turn that ends on an unaddressed one, are both right for an unattended launch and wrong for an attended one — a human session that cannot ask, or whose every question-ending turn gets bounced back, is worse off, not safer. settings.json.example is COPY, meant for every project alike; this file is the launch-time choices the kit ships pre-made, activated only when the operator passes it.",

  "_HOW_A_HEADLESS_SESSION_GETS_ITS_ALLOW_RULES": "A headless `claude -p` session does not apply the `permissions.allow` rules in a project's `.claude/settings.json` (its hooks do load, and a rule in the same file is not applied whether the file is tracked or not); it does apply rules from `.claude/settings.local.json`, from a `--settings <file>` and from `--allowedTools`. Give an unattended launch its allow rules through one of those three; the session must be able to Write the hat file (process/contracts/role-gate.md) or the role gate refuses every mutation.",

  "_WHAT_THIS_DOES_NOT_DO": "It does not make a session ask nothing — it removes ONE route back to a blocked wait and catches ONE shape of stall. The session still needs `scripts/ask.sh` and a declared `principal:` (PROJECT.md § Who answers when nobody is watching) to have anywhere to put a question instead. The Stop hook judges only how the last turn's text ENDS (the last line, after stripping Markdown emphasis, ends in a literal \"?\") — a statement-shaped stall, or a question answered by a later statement in the same turn, is not caught.",

  "env": {
    "KIT_UNATTENDED": "1"
  },

  "permissions": {
    "deny": ["AskUserQuestion"]
  },

  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/hooks/stop-ask.sh\"" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
